WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:10.977
Hi, everybody.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.913
Welcome to "The Tonight Show
At Home Edition."

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.548
Guys, we had some
great news yesterday.

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:18.017
Our friends over at State Farm

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:20.920
said they will match
up to $100,000 of donations.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.288
So, if you're
on YouTube right now,

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:27.126
click that button, donate
to redcross.org/statefarm.

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:28.594
Our neighbors
over at State Farm,

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:30.629
thank you, thank you so much,
for doing this.

00:00:30.629 --> 00:00:32.832
It's the coolest thing

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:36.502
and I just love how everyone's
just helping out.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:37.904
It's just really amazing.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:40.039
Speaking of helping out,
I wanted to say,

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:41.808
we talked yesterday
about Steve Higgins' daughter.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.209
Anna Higgins is a nurse

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.011
and we thanked her
for all she does,

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:47.313
but, to every nurse out there,
I really wanna say

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.881
thank you so much
for what you're doing.

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:52.485
You guys are on the front lines
and the doctors as well.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.821
You're heroes, so,
thank you, guys, so much.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.622
We have a fun show tonight.

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:59.659
My pal, my BFF,
Demi Lovato is on the show.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.660
What?!

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.794
She is the greatest.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:02.795
We're gonna talk to her.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:03.796
We're gonna have
a little art class,

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:06.198
a little painting lesson,
with Demi.

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:07.267
She's been doing
a lotta painting

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.235
and I'm gonna try
a self-portrait with her.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.004
And then, she's gonna sing
her new song,

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:14.340
"I Love Me,"
to close out the show tonight.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.308
And it's a beautiful song
with a great message

00:01:16.308 --> 00:01:18.344
and she can do it all.
She's great.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:21.815
Also, I have Jonathan Van Ness
is on the show.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:25.951
He has a children's book called
"Peanut Goes for the Gold"

00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:28.154
and it is about a...

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:31.991
nonbinary guinea pig

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:37.063
who wants to win the gold medal
in rhythmic gymnastics.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.498
So, it's one of those books.

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:42.535
"Oh, seen that one before,
yeah, obviously."

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:45.304
[chuckle]
It's so great to talk to him

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:47.440
and we'll find out
their charities,

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.642
which we have right here,
actually.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:52.712 line:0%
This is Demi Lovato's charity.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.147 line:0%
Winnie wrote this out. We'll
-Mm.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.282 line:0%
-maybe do a chyron for ya
so you can see.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.318 line:0%
#cut50.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:01.320 line:0%
It's a petition for you to sign,

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.190 line:0%
basically,

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.927 line:0%
raising awareness for prisoners
and people incarcerated

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:11.030 line:0%
that need help
during this time as well.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.332 line:0%
A little criminal justice there.

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:19.205 line:0%
And then, right here, this is
aliforneycenter.org.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.941 line:0%
And this is more
of a New York, local charity

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:24.310 line:0%
that Jonathan will talk
about later in the show.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.579
But I appreciate it.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:28.847
Guys, let's do
a little monologue.

00:02:28.847 --> 00:02:31.250
We did it yesterday
from the lemonade stand,

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.619
so, now, we graduate
and we have a real, actual,

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:34.820
working desk.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.622
Look how exciting this is.

00:02:36.622 --> 00:02:37.724
Wow.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:43.863
So. It's a little rickety,
but this is it right here.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.965
My camera operator is my wife.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.633
Nancy, I love you so much.

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:49.702
If you want to,
you can zoom in a little bit.

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.637
Gary, I guess you wanna
come in, too.

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:53.306
Okay.
-Hi, Gar.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:56.009
-Gary, you wanna be a guest?

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:57.109
-Higgins.

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:58.111
-C'mere, Gar.
[snaps fingers]

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.145
-[Laughs]
[ Thud ]

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:01.647
Good girl. Alright.

00:03:01.647 --> 00:03:03.182
Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:04.984
"At Home Edition."
It's a fun day in our house

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:07.520
'cause I decided to cook up
a real special meal.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.222
[ Smoke alarm beeping ]

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:11.124
Welcome to "The Tonight Show
At Home Edition."

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:13.793
It's a fun day in our house
'cause it's pizza night!

00:03:16.328 --> 00:03:17.596
What a show we have
for you guys.

00:03:17.596 --> 00:03:19.299
Demi Lovato
and Jonathan Van Ness

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:21.034
are my guests tonight
and who knows?

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.937
Maybe the My Pillow guy will
drop in for no reason at all.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.041
Did you see that yet, honey?

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.909
Oh, yeah.
I saw it, too.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.177
Let's get to some news.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:33.613
A Navy hospital ship
has arrived in New York

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.981
because, if there's one thing
we've learned from the crisis,

00:03:35.981 --> 00:03:39.418
it's that you definitely want
to be on a giant ship.

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:40.586
Well, this is nice.

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:41.787
Last night,
the Empire State Building

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:44.324
was lit up in red-and-white
flashing lights

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:45.892
to honor healthcare workers.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:47.393
When they saw that,
New Yorkers were like,

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.594
"That's great.

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:50.930
Maybe next time,
could you give us a heads up?!"

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:55.601
What?! I thought we were being
invaded by North Korea!

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:58.504
The flash-- I didn't even
know it could do that!

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.205
[ Laughing ]

00:04:00.205 --> 00:04:03.309
Gosh! Warn me.
Warn me, folks.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.310
Yep, everyone was confused

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.644
by the red-and-white
flashing lights.

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:07.080
At first, New Yorkers
thought it meant

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.516
Target finally got a shipment
[laughing] of toilet paper.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.318
I saw that there's
a Microsoft Excel

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:15.321
training program
now available for $49.99.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.823
Yep, I'm "three weeks
of isolation" bored,

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:20.994
but I'm not quite "Microsoft
Excel training" bored.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.130
This year, you can order --

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.932
I saw, this year, you can order
Girl Scout Cookies online.

00:04:26.932 --> 00:04:28.000
That's awesome.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.535
And, to give you
the real experience,

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:32.171
after you buy two boxes,
a Girl Scout pops up onscreen

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:34.573
and guilts you
into buying two more.

00:04:34.573 --> 00:04:36.241
[ Laughs ]

00:04:36.241 --> 00:04:38.077
-[Chuckle]

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.445
-I guess.
What's another box of

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:41.380
[Southern accent] Thin Mints?!

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.749
Gimme a Thin Mint!

00:04:43.749 --> 00:04:45.417
[own accent] I heard people
have been passing the time

00:04:45.417 --> 00:04:47.620
by stress baking,

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.289
which is just like regular
baking, except, when it's done,

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:51.858
you eat all of it
over the sink.

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:54.560
[ Laughing ]

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.362
And, finally, in Australia,

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:59.298
an astrophysicist got magnets
stuck up his nose

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:00.999
while trying to invent a device

00:05:00.999 --> 00:05:03.469
to stop people
from touching their faces.

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.770
That story again.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:07.673
Hey, Winnie and Frannie,
you both have what it takes

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:09.275
to be astrophysicists!

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:10.342
-[Laughing]

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:12.177
-And that's our monologue
for tonight.

00:05:12.177 --> 00:05:14.012
Guys, you've been sending in
great questions called

00:05:14.012 --> 00:05:15.714
#AskTheFallons,

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:18.417
and questions you wanna
ask my wife, Nancy;

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:20.853
or my daughters,
Winnie and Frannie.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:24.023
So, we went for a social
distancing walk today

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:26.325
and had a couple
nice discussions.

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:28.327
Please enjoy.

00:05:28.327 --> 00:05:30.762
Okay, so this is
interview number 2.

00:05:30.762 --> 00:05:32.531
Are those my sunglasses?
-No.

00:05:32.531 --> 00:05:35.635
Yes, I only own
your sunglasses.

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:37.102
-Isn't it funny?

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:40.939
Sometimes we don't even
practice it or whatever,

00:05:40.939 --> 00:05:44.844
talk about it, plan it, but we
wear the same things sometimes.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.511
Stripey shirt or...
-Yeah.

00:05:46.511 --> 00:05:48.347
Or like Navy sweaters.

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:50.816
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.816 --> 00:05:52.551
We're looking like we're
getting ready for a bad,

00:05:52.551 --> 00:05:54.654
-Yeah.
-awkward, family portrait.

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:56.155
-Yep.

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:57.656
-How's homeschooling,
by the way?

00:05:57.656 --> 00:06:00.392
It's been fun.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:06:00.392 --> 00:06:01.393
[gasp] Here comes a van.

00:06:01.393 --> 00:06:02.695
Don't say anything.

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:04.296
-[Laughs]

00:06:04.296 --> 00:06:05.297
-But we're gonna wave.

00:06:05.297 --> 00:06:08.067
Hi!

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:10.369
Homeschooling?

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:13.605
These teachers are brilliant.

00:06:13.605 --> 00:06:15.774
-Amazing.
-Devoted, loyal.

00:06:15.774 --> 00:06:19.444
They are just going
so out of their way

00:06:19.444 --> 00:06:22.014
to make this okay
for those of us

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:24.984
[laughing] who do not know
what we're doing.

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:26.051
Raising hand high.

00:06:26.051 --> 00:06:28.454
And we're getting through it.

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:29.488
Here we go.

00:06:29.488 --> 00:06:30.856
-Are you getting better
at Zoom?

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:32.725
-I am getting -ish.

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:34.327
I still fight it,
but I keep saying,

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:37.262
about this whole virus thing,
"Stop fighting it.

00:06:37.262 --> 00:06:39.532
Stop fighting the change.

00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:41.734
Stop fighting the new
way of life, for now.

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:46.939
Just go with it and I think
will help you mentally."

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:49.909
-Okay, these are questions
people wanna know

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:51.510
or wanted me to ask you.
-Okay.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.246
-"What's your favorite
memory with Gary?"

00:06:54.246 --> 00:06:56.849
