And then, when I really
developed a crush

00:10:12.745 --> 00:10:16.915
was when Bradley Thomas'
kids came to set

00:10:16.915 --> 00:10:18.250
and he had a little girl
named Lucy

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:19.784
and a little boy named Charlie.

00:10:19.784 --> 00:10:22.755
And I played with Lucy
and Jimmy played with Charlie

00:10:22.755 --> 00:10:24.590
and really played,

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:28.360
like really into it,
as if they'd come to visit us.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:31.496
And so I think that's
when my heart just sort of

00:10:31.496 --> 00:10:32.798
melted
[Southern accent] even more.

00:10:32.798 --> 00:10:34.733
-Aw.
I remember those kids.

00:10:34.733 --> 00:10:36.635
Oh, they were so cute.
-Yeah.

00:10:36.635 --> 00:10:38.837
They're like teenagers, now,
or in college, probably.

00:10:38.837 --> 00:10:42.241
-I remember when I first

00:10:42.241 --> 00:10:47.346
experienced the magic that is
[chuckle] Nancy Juvonen.

00:10:47.346 --> 00:10:48.547
We were on the set,

00:10:48.547 --> 00:10:50.816
but we were filming
"Fever Pitch" in Boston

00:10:50.816 --> 00:10:54.186
-Yeah.
-and it was a rainy,

00:10:54.186 --> 00:10:56.121
gray, Bostony day.

00:10:56.121 --> 00:10:59.191
-Yep.
-And you came to set.

00:10:59.191 --> 00:11:00.592
And you --
-I walked to set.

00:11:00.592 --> 00:11:02.028
That was the first day
of shooting.

00:11:02.028 --> 00:11:03.094
-Yeah.

00:11:03.094 --> 00:11:04.163
And you walked to set

00:11:04.163 --> 00:11:06.164
and I wanna say
you had white pants,

00:11:06.164 --> 00:11:07.800
-Yes.
-a pink sweater...

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:08.800
-[Laughing]

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:11.470
-...and a green backpack?
-Yeah, my

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:13.606
green Jansport backpack...

00:11:13.606 --> 00:11:14.707
[ Laughter ]

00:11:14.707 --> 00:11:16.341
...that I think I'd had
since college.

00:11:16.341 --> 00:11:18.844
-And blond hair
and your white teeth.

00:11:18.844 --> 00:11:21.980
And I was like you just stood
out in this gray --

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:23.749
It was almost like a painting.

00:11:23.749 --> 00:11:26.518
And you stood out like a neon --

00:11:26.518 --> 00:11:29.621
And I was like, "Uh, wow.

00:11:29.621 --> 00:11:32.624
She is," yeah.
You just stuck out.

00:11:32.624 --> 00:11:34.994
And you were just so fun.
We had so much fun

00:11:34.994 --> 00:11:36.562
on that movie, didn't we?
-Yeah. We had so much fun,

00:11:36.562 --> 00:11:38.464
And we got to just

00:11:38.464 --> 00:11:40.799
sort of flirt and hang out
and get to know each other,

00:11:40.799 --> 00:11:44.470
without having to go on a date
or anything like that.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:47.572
-No.
-For months!
We just got to be pals.

00:11:47.572 --> 00:11:49.175
-Yeah.
-And have crushes,

00:11:49.175 --> 00:11:51.810
which is so hard and so fun,

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:54.479
and it shouldn't just be
limited to high school.

00:11:54.479 --> 00:11:55.648
-Right?
-It's so fun to have

00:11:55.648 --> 00:11:57.650
to kind of wait and just like,
"Oo-oo-ooh!

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:58.751
What should I wear
[singsong] today?

00:11:58.751 --> 00:11:59.951
Is he gonna be on set early?

00:11:59.951 --> 00:12:01.253
What's gonna happen?

00:12:01.253 --> 00:12:02.620
[ Laughter ]

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:04.223
Is he shooting today?"

00:12:04.223 --> 00:12:07.192
-Yeah. But we got to know each
other's musical taste and --

00:12:07.192 --> 00:12:09.327
-Yeah, and then,
when the show ended,

00:12:09.327 --> 00:12:12.130
we weren't sure, like,
"Maybe this is nothing.

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:14.366
Maybe this is just
a cute little flirt."

00:12:14.366 --> 00:12:17.135
And I'm like, "He's probably
dating like 30 women.

00:12:17.135 --> 00:12:18.804
I don't know."

00:12:18.804 --> 00:12:20.206
I know now how funny that is,

00:12:20.206 --> 00:12:21.807
but, at the time, I didn't know.

00:12:21.807 --> 00:12:24.476
[ Laughter ]
-Gosh! Dating 30 women?

00:12:24.476 --> 00:12:26.745
Oh, my God.
-I don't know what people do.

00:12:26.745 --> 00:12:28.180
-I know.
I'm like Pete the Pilot.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:30.982
-Yeah.
Totally were The Bachelor.

00:12:30.982 --> 00:12:34.219
And then, you know, I'm sure he
didn't know what I was up to.

00:12:34.219 --> 00:12:35.421
-Yeah.
-And then, when we saw

00:12:35.421 --> 00:12:36.689
each other again...
-In London.

00:12:36.689 --> 00:12:38.924
-In London.
-We were selling the movie.

00:12:38.924 --> 00:12:41.060
-To sell the movie.
-I was like, "Hey!

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:42.861
I miss you.

00:12:42.861 --> 00:12:45.197
I wanna hang out with you."
-Mm-hmm.

00:12:45.197 --> 00:12:46.832
-And then, you said
you missed me, too.

00:12:46.832 --> 00:12:48.467
[ Laughter ]

00:12:48.467 --> 00:12:51.536
Corny. This is gonna be
the corniest video

00:12:51.536 --> 00:12:53.738
that anybody's ever seen.

00:12:53.738 --> 00:12:57.876
Alright, that's enough
#AskTheFallons for now, right?

00:12:57.876 --> 00:13:00.045
-It's a good session, I think.
-It's a good session.

00:13:00.045 --> 00:13:01.413
[ Laughter ]
It's a good session.

00:13:01.413 --> 00:13:03.382
We'll be right back, everybody.
-Bye!

